From 81c34c56d39d52e368ab03df325474bcc4ab1750 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:16:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(flowchart): a curve swinging into its head runs
 straight in, no S or hump (B1 review r3 #3, Q1+M1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Report §2.3. The straight entry of square_end (the head of a curve that
turns too hard over its last stretch to bend into a run within a px)
left the curve at the least-stray sample within two heads, at an angle
to the line it then drew: its cubic inflected (an S where it left the
curve) and, on a shallow curve hooking onto a side, rose into a hump
before the head (dense-td n16->n23, n5->n7, n7->n33; bench-75 db->svc2,
cache->svc4, queue->metrics; a thick ==> into a fan; fanout-frames
n0->g1 rose vertically into a right-pointing head).

Now it leaves the curve where the line from the corner under the head
touches it most nearly (within SQUARE_END_ARC; the point nearest the
end within SQUARE_END_TOUCH = 5 deg of that, so the line stays short),
and runs on straight into the head; a line straying over
SQUARE_END_MAX_STRAY there tries 10 and 20 deg before the least-stray
search. A curve that slips in under the head first is kept up to there
and joined to the run inside the triangle (no stray at all). Heads stay
square with the tip on the border; outside the head the stroke keeps
within the stray bound picking relies on.

The angle the stroke meets a square head at is the scene curve's own:
fanout-frames n0->g1 is an LR S-cubic with 23 px handles over a 351 px
rise (tangent() caps a handle at half the gap so the cubic stays
monotone), 27 px off its end tangent one head back — no cubic between
those ends arrives straight without overshooting; that needs the edge's
shape (stubs and a spline), outside the painter. So the SVG-level count
of ends meeting the head base > 20 deg off is unchanged (bench-75 17 |
29, dense-td 18 | 28); what changed is the S and the hump (new test).

Speed: only the bound is asked of the chosen entry and of the smooth
bends (stray_within: a point clears on the first segment within the
limit); the tail is measured only as far back as candidates reach; the
tail is sampled every 1 px (SQUARE_END_STEP 0.5 -> 1.0, entry step
4 -> 2 samples; bends keep 24 steps). to_svg instructions, pre-B1 ->
e0a63d2 -> a0a2314 -> now: synth1000 179M -> (8x) -> 378M -> 326M;
bench-75 26.9M -> 30.4M; dense-td 13.4M -> 16.4M. perf.sh within
budget.

Tests: a_curve_swinging_in_from_the_side_enters_its_head_straight (no
heading swing back beyond SQUARE_END_TOUCH and no hump outside the
head, head square, run on the tangent, stray bound) on the n0->g1 cubic,
a shallow hook and a symmetric S. Byte-exact snapshots unchanged.

Gates (tests/quality.rs): DEFECT_BASELINE lowered — end_kink 62|81 ->
60|77, band_len routed 46 610 -> 46 604, x_drawn routed 521 -> 520.
BORDER_LEN_MAX static 1070 -> 1082 (raised, reason in its comment): two
bench-75 ends just inside the data frame (svc3->db, user->gw) now enter
along the touching line instead of an S hugging their curve, 9 and 3 px
longer within reach of the frame's left border; no route changed.

